# What the routes ask of the machine they run on, as data and one record of
# functions. A route turns a request into a `Job` (the heavy part: stage the
# source, run the compilers, run the program) and hands it to a `Host`, which
# decides where the job runs and under what limit. The two entries differ
# exactly there, so the routes (play/routes) are written once:
#
#   - main.dawn, the long-lived web server on the JVM, runs a job in the same
#     process under an in-process permit and keeps a process-local answer cache
#     (play/jvmhost, the only module that still needs `use java`);
#   - serve, one process per request, runs a job in a child process that holds
#     a cross-process flock permit for as long as it runs, and keeps no cache
#     (play/gate). There is no process to hold a cache in, and the ruling on
#     the native runner dropped it until the logs show repeated compiles worth
#     a file cache.
#
# Why a record of functions and not an interface of two modules: the choice is
# made once, at the entry, and the routes below it never learn which one they
# got, which is what keeps `use java` out of everything the native entry
# imports. The job is a closed set of cases and not a closure for the same
# reason: a closure cannot cross into another process, a value can be written
# to a file.
use play/contract.{Outcome}
use play/exec.{ViewRaw}

## The heavy part of one request. `native` is whether `dawnc` may be used.
pub type Job =
  | JRun(code: String)
  | JCheck(code: String, native: Bool)
  | JView(code: String, native: Bool)
  | JTile(code: String)

## What a job came to. `JBroken` is a job that did not come back at all (the
## child died or wrote nothing): the route answers 500 with the message.
pub type JobResult =
  | JOutcome(outcome: Outcome)
  | JViewRaw(raw: ViewRaw)
  | JBroken(message: String)

## `call(wait_secs, job)` runs the job once a permit is free, waiting up to
## `wait_secs` for one; None means the machine stayed saturated and the route
## answers 429. `keep_get` and `keep_put` are the answer cache.
pub type Host = {
  call: fn(Int, Job) -> Option[JobResult] !io,
  keep_get: fn(String) -> Option[String] !io,
  keep_put: fn(String, String) -> Unit !io,
}

## The cache of a host that keeps none.
pub fn no_keep_get(_key: String) -> Option[String] = None

pub fn no_keep_put(_key: String, _text: String) -> Unit = ()
